{number: 54}
{title: We Have Heard the Joyful Sound}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] We have heard the joyful sound: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
Spread the tidings all a-[D7] round: Jesus saves! [G] Jesus saves!
Bear the [C] news to every [G] land, climb the [C] steeps and cross the [G] waves;
Onward! 'tis our Lord's com-[D7] mand: Jesus [G] saves! [D7] Jesus [G] saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Waft it on the rolling tide: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
Tell to sinners far and [D7] wide: Jesus saves! [G] Jesus saves!
Sing, ye [C] islands of the [G] sea; echo [C] back, ye ocean [G] caves;
Earth shall keep her jubi-[D7] lee: Jesus [G] saves! [D7] Jesus [G] saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Sing above the battle strife: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
By His death and endless [D7] life: Jesus saves! [G] Jesus saves!
Sing it [C] softly through the [G] gloom, when the [C] heart for mercy [G] craves;
Sing in triumph o'er the [D7] tomb: Jesus [G] saves! [D7] Jesus [G] saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[G] Give the winds a mighty voice: Jesus saves! Jesus saves!
Let the nations now re-[D7] joice: Jesus saves! [G] Jesus saves!
Shout sal-[C] vation full and [G] free to the [C] utmost of the [G] waves;
This our song of victo-[D7] ry: Jesus [G] saves! [D7] Jesus [G] saves!
{end_of_verse}
